course: dictionary
lesson: 2248
title: Cramp: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around a word show you which meaning the writer means. Read the whole sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits. «A cramp is a muscle squeezing hard and not letting go» tells you that here cramp is about muscles.
explain: Look at the clues. «Night cramp in the calf is common and usually harmless» is about the leg, so a cramp is a painful tightening of a muscle. «Cramp is a muscle suddenly tightening and not relaxing» says the same thing in other words.
explain: Cramp can be a noun, a thing you get, or a verb, an action. To cramp someone means to stop them moving or acting freely, as in cramp your style. Cramped is a different word: a cramped room is crowded, with no space to move.
fact: A cramp is a sudden, painful tightening of a muscle, often in the leg or foot.
fact: Cramp can also mean pains in the stomach, as in stomach cramps.
fact: Cramp is common after exercise, and tired muscles cramp more easily.
fact: Gently stretching the muscle usually helps, and drinking water can help too.
fact: A cramp usually passes in minutes, though the muscle can ache afterwards.
exercise: «A cramp is a muscle squeezing hard and not letting go.» What is a cramp? | A type of sports shoe | A loud noise in the playground | *A sudden, painful tightening of a muscle | A small, cosy room with no windows
exercise: «Night cramp in the calf is common and usually harmless.» Where is the cramp? | In the ears when it is cold | In the head, behind the eyes | *In the calf, at the back of the leg | On the top of the hand
exercise: «The tight rules began to cramp her style.» What does cramp mean here? | *To stop someone moving or acting freely | To tidy up a messy room | To make someone laugh loudly | To pack a bag quickly
test: «Her stomach cramps made her lie down.» What does cramps mean here? | A loud noise from the kitchen | *Pains in the stomach | Hiccups that won't stop | Feeling sleepy after lunch
test: «The little bus was cramped, with people squeezed in everywhere.» What does cramped mean? | Cold and damp | Bright and sunny | Clean and shiny | *Crowded, with no room to move
exam: Which sentence uses cramp to mean stop someone moving or acting freely? | Stretch your calf if a cramp hits. | *The tight rules began to cramp her style. | I had a cramp in my foot during the race.
